;; CG8 graduation compatibility promise (2026-08-17): `cycle-gc` graduated, so
;; its EXPERIMENTS[] row is gone -- but a downstream `build.tur`,
;; `~/.config/turmeric/experiments.tur`, or CLI invocation that still names it
;; must keep compiling.  `GRADUATED[]` in src/runtime/experiments.c is what
;; makes `--enable=cycle-gc` a TUR-W0063 no-op instead of the hard TUR-E0310 an
;; unknown experiment name gets.
;;
;; Without this fixture graduation is a breaking change for exactly the people
;; who adopted the feature deliberately, which is the wrong population to
;; break.  The flag is in `flags`; the warning is asserted on stderr and
;; (gc-auto!) elaborates with no flag needed at all.
;;
;; What graduated is the CALL FORM, not a default.  `gc-auto-collects-without-
;; gc-call` is the fixture that pins what AUTO does once you ask for it; this
;; one only pins that asking no longer needs an experiment flag, and that a
;; lingering flag is tolerated.
(defn main [] : int
  (gc-auto!)
  (println "cycle-gc-graduated-enable-noop")
  0)
